<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brigade</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as brigades</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A brigade is a military formation made up of several battalions or regiments, smaller than a division. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> reorganised the massive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tercio">tercio</a> squares into smaller, more manoeuvrable brigades of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pike">pikemen</a>. At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Adwa</a> in 1896, the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> destroyed three Italian brigades.</p></div>
